<title>SPAIN: TABLE-Santander H1 net attributable up 30.2 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Santander H1 net attributable up 30.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Santander banking group six months through June (billion pesetas, unless stated)</p>
<p> Net attributable profit		59.78   vs	45.90</p>
<p> Net interest income		   238.83   vs     191.78</p>
<p> Ordinary income			 383.28   vs     303.92</p>
<p> Operating income			115.02   vs	93.60</p>
<p> Pretax profit			   109.83   vs	83.88</p>
<p> Net income				 82.35   vs	62.91</p>
<p> Adj. net attributable income	 72.05   vs	54.89</p>
<p>NOTE: Adjusted net attributable income excludes goodwill amortisation.</p>
<p> Interest income			 805.56   vs  754.11</p>
<p> Equity-accounted dividends	    8.51   vs   11.11</p>
<p> Interest expenses		     575.24   vs  573.45</p>
